.TH FANFOLD 1 "" "Fan Fold 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fanfold \- edge-fan Markdown notes over an ordinary folder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fanfold
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Fan Fold
is a Qt 6 desktop note shell that edits ordinary Markdown files in a folder
chosen by the user. Notes are never copied into an application database, so the
folder remains readable, searchable and syncable by any other tool.
.PP
The window rests at the screen edge and fans the notes out as overlapping
cards. It provides a recursive library with search, bounded offline rich-text
editors, autosave with conflict recovery, archive and restore, desktop trash,
movable pinned note windows, per-note paper and ink colours, and global
typography and layout settings.
.PP
On first run Fan Fold asks which folder of Markdown files to open. That choice
is remembered; no pre-existing file is moved, rewritten or converted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-root " folder"
Open this folder of Markdown notes instead of the remembered one. The folder is
read and written in place.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " folder"
Use this directory for application state instead of the XDG data home. This
redirects the document index, fan order, per-note metadata and crash-recovery
journal, and is intended for isolated or disposable runs.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/FanFold/
Settings, including the remembered notes folder, plus
.IR appearance.json .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/FanFold/
Document index, fan order, per-note metadata and the crash-recovery journal.
Overridden by
.BR \-\-state .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/FanFold/
Disposable Qt and QtWebEngine cache data.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fanfold/
Installed QML shell, editor bridge and the vendored offline editor runtime.
.PP
Notes themselves live only in the folder the user selected. Removing the
package leaves that folder, and everything above under the user's home
directory, untouched.
.SH NETWORK
Fan Fold performs no network access of its own. The editor runtime is vendored
and loaded from the local filesystem; no content is fetched from a CDN at
startup or during editing.
.SH SEE ALSO
The installed third-party inventory at
.I /usr/share/doc/fanfold/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
and the licence texts under
.IR /usr/share/doc/fanfold/licenses/ .
